Significance: patch
Type: fixed

Preserve the persisted AT Protocol identity when disconnecting so the `.well-known/atproto-did` route keeps serving. Sites that adopted a custom domain handle (`example.com` instead of `alice.bsky.social`) could not reconnect after a disconnect because the wiped identity left the well-known route 404'ing, and the handle resolver had nothing to find. Disconnect now drops only the OAuth session; reconnecting refreshes identity in place.
